# Docs examples: no TypeScript typings

Code under `src/docs/examples/` is loaded into a live interpreter. Typings crash it.

Do **not** add:

- Type annotations (`const x: string`, `(name: string) =>`)
- `interface` / `type` aliases
- `as` casts (`as const`, `as Option[]`)
- Generics on hooks/JSX (`useState<string>`, `<Foo<T>>`)
- Typed imports used only for types

Write JS-friendly untyped code, same style as `Button/Simple.tsx` and `TextShimmer/Example.tsx`.

```tsx
// BAD
const [size, setSize] = useState<string>('m');
function toggleGroup(name: string) {}

// GOOD
const [size, setSize] = useState('m');
function toggleGroup(name) {}
```

`index.tsx` page shells (docs copy, `TypesTable`) can stay typed. `*.styl.d.ts` is generated — leave it.
